repository-code: "https://github.com/TheWa1kingDead/Three-Dimensional-Nozzle-Design-Code"
license: NASA-1.3
abstract: >-
  A maintained edition of NASA's Three-Dimensional Nozzle Design Code (NASA
  software designation LEW-20180, originally developed by T. Rice at JHU/APL).
  It contains three MFC applications for supersonic nozzle design: a 2D/axisymmetric
  method-of-characteristics grid generator (MOC_Grid_BDE), a streamline tracing
  tool (STT2001), and a 3D method-of-characteristics flowfield solver (3D_MOC).
  This edition corrects the transonic throat (initial data line) solutions of
  Hall (1962) and Kliegel & Levine (1969) used in MOC_Grid_BDE, fixes an
  iteration-guard bug, and provides Visual Studio 2022+ projects that build
  standalone Windows executables.
keywords:
  - method of characteristics
  - supersonic nozzle design
  - rocket nozzle
  - streamline tracing
  - transonic throat flow
  - compressible flow
  - Rao nozzle
